{
  "about": [
    "Conformance cases for commerce sale events, contract version 1. TypeScript runs them with zod and with ajv against the JSON Schema (shared/events/financial-events/tests/commerce-sale-v1.test.ts); Python runs them against the accounting consumer's contract mirror (foundational/accounting/tests/test_commerce_posting_contract.py). All data is synthetic.",
    "valid: events every implementation accepts unchanged, with the S10 replayDigest each must compute. Their ids and aggregate ids are the S1 and S2 vectors.",
    "invalid: a valid event and a patch (RFC 6902 add, replace or remove; the path '' replaces the whole document). rule 'schema' means the JSON Schema rejects it; a rule id S1-S8 means the JSON Schema accepts it and the contract implementations reject it with an error naming that rule first. Each case breaks exactly one rule.",
    "refundAgainstSale: S7, which needs the stored sale: the sale given must be the one the refund names, and match it. A patch applies to the refund; rule null means the refund matches its sale.",
    "uuidV5: UUIDv5(namespace, name) vectors for provider key shapes the events above do not cover.",
    "Values only: these cases are JSON values, so they hold no number written with a fraction or exponent and no duplicate key. Event JSON text must not contain either (a reader rejects 2000.0, which JavaScript's JSON.parse cannot tell from 2000); the TypeScript producer writes canonical JSON lines, and the Python reader refuses both."
  ],
  "schema": "../../schema/commerce-sale-events.v1.schema.json",
  "namespace": "6f1d3c52-8a4e-4d7b-9c1e-2b5a7e9f0c31",
